{
  "case_id": "2017-17-130",
  "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mark Perry",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "SEC ALJs have been invested with the sovereign power to preside over formal adjudications. They are officers under all of this Court's precedents, particularly Freytag and Edmond, and any textually and historically accurate construction of the Appointments Clause, which -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Inferior officers -- you're not contesting that -- that they are more than inferior officers?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry, that -\u00ad that figure is somewhat misleading."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Everything is manipulable. But -- but our -- our founding fathers designated some people employees and others not, serving somewhat similar functions or not, so that we can't really go by the founding fathers' practices because they were rather mixed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Metlitsky (Amicus)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "historically-grounded exception concerning diplomatic offices, an officer of the United States is someone with power to bind the government or private parties in the name of his own office. In contrast, someone whose acts have no binding effect without the sanction of an officer is not himself an officer of the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Metlitsky (Amicus)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. METLITSKY: So, as we acknowledged in our brief, you could read Freytag broadly, obviously, much more broadly than the rule we're proposing, but you don't have to read it that way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Okay. Let's take an Assistant Attorney General. I assume that that person is an officer of the United States, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Metlitsky",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. METLITSKY: No. So -- so they are not officers for -- for two reasons: One is that they don't have, in our view, decisions to make binding -- the authority to make binding decisions in the first place."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Just so I understand, what would this do with already completed cases -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 706 of the APA says that upon a finding of constitutional violation, the reviewing court shall set aside all actions, findings, and conclusions of the agency, which means they all have to be wiped out because there was a constitutional violation here, start from scratch, or, as we suggest, dismiss the OIP."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Metlitsky",
      "case_id": "2017-17-130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c3cd057013ddccfab0e8e102d310c2c0afb6db016a0b79dd5f125f0bff68283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c3cd057013d-0003-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Metlitsky, this Court appointed you to brief and argue this case as amicus curiae in support of the judgment -- judgment below. You have ably discharged that responsibility, for which we are grateful."
    },
